1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Section 2

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,950
Good morning everyone.

3
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:09,580
My name's Janet Parker and I'm the human resources manager.

4
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:13,672
We're very happy to welcome you to your new apprenticeship.

5
00:00:13,672 --> 00:00:18,174
I hope that the next six months will be a positive

6
00:00:18,174 --> 00:00:20,220
and enjoyable experience for you.

7
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:25,780
I'd like to start with some general advice about being an apprentice.

8
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:32,230
Most of you have very little or no experience of working for a big organisation

9
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:36,530
and the first week or so may be quite challenging.

10
00:00:36,530 --> 00:00:40,967
There will be a lot of new information to take in

11
00:00:40,967 --> 00:00:45,000
but don't worry too much about trying to remember everything.

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,323
The important thing is to check with someone if you're not sure what to

13
00:00:51,323 --> 00:00:57,194
do - you'll find your supervisor is very approachable and won't mind explaining things

14
00:00:57,194 --> 00:00:59,000
or helping you out.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
You're here to learn so make the most of that opportunity.

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,632
You'll be spending time in different departments during your first week

17
00:01:08,632 --> 00:01:14,526
so make an effort to talk to as many people as possible about their

18
00:01:14,526 --> 00:01:20,000
work - you'll make some new friends and find out lots of useful information.

19
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,560
As well as having a supervisor, you'll each be assigned a mentor.

20
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:30,002
This person will be someone who's recently completed an apprenticeship

21
00:01:30,002 --> 00:01:34,000
and you'll meet with them on a weekly basis.

22
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,410
Their role is to provide help and support throughout your apprenticeship.

23
00:01:39,410 --> 00:01:44,991
Of course, this doesn't mean they actually do any of your work for you

24
00:01:44,991 --> 00:01:48,978
- instead they'll be asking you about what goals you've achieved

25
00:01:48,978 --> 00:01:54,160
so far, as well as helping you to identify any areas for improvement.

26
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:59,500
You can also discuss your more long-term ambitions with them as well.

27
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:06,107
Now I just want to run through a few company policies for our apprenticeship

28
00:02:06,107 --> 00:02:07,522
scheme with you.

29
00:02:07,522 --> 00:02:09,410
Most importantly, the internet.

30
00:02:09,410 --> 00:02:14,344
As part of your job you'll be doing some research online

31
00:02:14,344 --> 00:02:20,623
so obviously you'll have unlimited access for that but please don't use it for

32
00:02:20,623 --> 00:02:24,660
personal use - you'll have your own phones for that.

33
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:29,270
Some of you have already asked me about flexible working.

34
00:02:29,270 --> 00:02:35,180
After your probationary three-month period - some of you will be eligible for this -

35
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:41,545
but it will depend on which department you're in and what your personal circumstances

36
00:02:41,545 --> 00:02:42,000
are.

37
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,570
So please don't assume you'll automatically be permitted to do this.

38
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:52,670
I want to make sure there's no confusion about our holiday policy.

39
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:59,817
Apart from any statutory public holidays we ask that you don't book any holidays

40
00:02:59,817 --> 00:03:03,390
until after your six-month apprenticeship has finished.

41
00:03:03,390 --> 00:03:07,307
Time off should only be taken if you are unwell.

42
00:03:07,307 --> 00:03:12,400
Please speak to your supervisor if this is going to be a problem.

43
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:19,297
You'll be expected to work a 40-hour week but there may be opportunities to

44
00:03:19,297 --> 00:03:21,760
do overtime during busy periods.

45
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:27,147
Although you're not required to do this, it can be a valuable experience -

46
00:03:27,147 --> 00:03:31,290
so we advise you to take it up if possible.

47
00:03:31,290 --> 00:03:35,876
Obviously, we understand that people do have commitments outside work,

48
00:03:35,876 --> 00:03:40,920
so don't worry if there are times when you are unavailable.

49
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:46,377
As you know, we don't have a formal dress code here - you may

50
00:03:46,377 --> 00:03:51,833
wear casual clothes as long as they're practical - and the only restriction for

51
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:56,870
shoes we have is on high heels for health and safety reasons.

52
00:03:56,870 --> 00:04:00,870
Comfortable shoes like trainers are preferable.

53
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:07,386
There's a heavily subsidised canteen on site where you can get hot meals

54
00:04:07,386 --> 00:04:08,890
or salads cheaply.

55
00:04:08,890 --> 00:04:15,731
Snacks and drinks are also provided - so we've decided to introduce a no

56
00:04:15,731 --> 00:04:17,310
packed lunch policy.

57
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:23,935
This is partly to encourage healthy eating at work and partly to stop people

58
00:04:23,935 --> 00:04:26,300
from eating at their workstation,

59
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:27,720
which is unhygienic.

60
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:31,000
OK moving on to...
